+
+The `fix.patch` used for 4b therefore contains the test-only change. There is no product hunk to reverse: the product
+class already has the correct behaviour, and changing it (for example by adding a Qt-6-only compatibility method just
+to satisfy a test) would add API for no user-visible reason. Reverting the test guard is the exact reproduction of the
+CI defect.
+
+## Self-check
+
+- **Regression fails without the fix and passes with it.** Qt 5 standalone build of the test source: without the
+  guard `EXIT=1` with the two exact CI errors (`qt5-build-2-red.log`); with the guard `EXIT=0` and 6/6 tests pass
+  (`qt5-test-3-green-restored.log`). The local Qt 6 build passes both ways because Qt 6 has the method; that is why
+  the platform-build leg is the meaningful RED/GREEN, not Qt 6.
+- **Deterministic.** Compile-time platform/API check plus direct model/view calls. No wall-clock timing, sleeps,
+  threads, races or randomness; no timestamps needed.
+- **Cause and completeness.** Checked every use of the API in the file (`grep` found only the two original calls) and
+  the class definition (`include/RowTableView.h:37` inherits `QTableView`, no override). The helper is the only
+  non-test-platform change; no sibling product path exists. The same helper covers both Qt 5 and Qt 6 builds.
+- **No collateral damage.** No production code, save format, project loader, command registry or audio code changed.
+  Old projects and saved data are untouched. No new limit or check was added.
+- **Realtime / undo / commands.** The diff is a test-only source file; nothing runs on the audio thread, and no
+  command, undo step or reversibility class changed.
+- **Old projects and round-trip.** Not applicable: no serialization, project model or product behaviour changed.
+- **GUI path.** The test drives the real `RowTableView` widget and a real `QStandardItemModel`; no handler or
+  registry shortcut is used. The insert path is exactly the delegate path that the test checks.
+- **Portability.** The change removes a Qt-6-only call from test source by guarding it with `QT_VERSION`; Qt 5.15 and
+  Qt 6 both compile it. No `windows.h`, no `std::filesystem`, no new platform assumption.
+- **Log-folder limitation.** The required log folder rejected writes with EACCES (`touch` EXIT=2; `write` tool EACCES)
+  before any command ran. I recorded every log under the ignored worktree directory
+  `build/qwen-logs-ci-a70284ef7d26941c/` instead, rather than omitting evidence.
+
+Files committed: `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp` and this report.
